                <pb facs="0531" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/26904: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-31T14:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                                1924—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:42 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram January 23, 5 p.m. All mines have been removed from ports
                    in question. Am informed by Mr. de la Huerta that Salina Cruz was mined by
                    Federal authorities. He feels that it was not asking too much in view of the
                    removal of this protection he had against an attack by the Mexican gunboat <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bravo</hi> now at New Orleans to entertain the hope that
                    said gunboat will not be allowed to leave the port of New Orleans during this
                    conflict.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
